70 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "3b3fc28f-36b5-5b87-bb0f-cb9b45688be1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050938 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050938 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050938 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050938 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050938 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050938 #edb/ref 1031 "Calculating the Dot Product Using Angle and Magnitude" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050938 #edb/ref 1033 243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050938 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "72f91576-0c59-56f1-b220-5c20b8f21c92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050988 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050988 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050988 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050988 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050988 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050988 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050988 #edb/ref 1031 "Calculating the Magnitude of Cartesian Vectors in 2D" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050988 #edb/ref 1033 176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050988 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "773e9f74-2606-5a7c-96ea-1dbef24812bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428198 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1031 "Calculating the Magnitude of Cartesian Vectors in 3D" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1033 1277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1034 0.7167474973411709 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7ab3215d-4ce4-5e76-8672-0d6b5580e957" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059527 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4297" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059527 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -4, 6 \\rangle$. Find $\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\, \\mid$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059527 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2b211fe-d37a-55dd-bf76-9ffab2b6f128" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059527 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a \\mid &= \\sqrt{a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-4)^{2} + (6)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16 + 36} \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059528 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4298" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059528 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A(1,3)$ and $B(2,-2)$. Find $\\mid \\overrightarrow{AB} \\mid$.\n\n![](images/f9/f95ee3c5c81750d97019d910350e4c78f0962baa682c834928450a451691145a.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059528 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d4ad6011-24a4-5642-997f-dcc4e807224f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059528 #edb/ref 1074 "We have\n\n$$\nOA^(→) = a = i + 3j,; OB^(→) = b = 2i - 2j\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB^(→) &= OB^(→) - OA^(→) \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (2i - 2j) - (i + 3j) \\\\\n&= i - 5j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid AB^(→) \\mid &= \\sqrt{1^{2} + (-5)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1 + 25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059530 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4301" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059530 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059530 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "65198cdd-dd3b-5840-aaf3-cecd96eb9d3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059530 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + 2b}{\\mid a + 2b \\mid}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na + 2b &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + 2 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 + 2 \\\\ 0 + (-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a + 2b \\mid &= \\sqrt{0^{2} + (-2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4} \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + 2b}{\\mid a + 2b \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(a + 2b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059714 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059714 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059714 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059714 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059714 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059714 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186501352 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186059714 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 175921