592186045417] [17592186059899 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186060593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059899 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186060594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059899 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186060596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059899 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059899 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating the Magnitude of Cartesian Vectors in 2D" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059899 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186060591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059899 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059899 #edb/ref 1050 540.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059899 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "83dac894-319c-5863-b45c-982a3ff6f9ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060591 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060591 #edb/ref 1061 15728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060591 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5b84d0dd-ba79-58a3-b448-a38e7315fb69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060591 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060592 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060592 #edb/ref 1061 15729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060592 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3e7af8b4-e759-5d78-9a44-b80a9db8a7f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060592 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060593 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060593 #edb/ref 1061 15730 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060593 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f09b880a-a7cb-5551-8c97-2db4d49a85e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060593 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060594 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060594 #edb/ref 1061 15731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060594 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22598683-ff99-58ac-947d-835cfc0c4788" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060594 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060596 #edb/ref 1061 15734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060596 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3859575a-3fa2-5c94-81ec-63f71bc687f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060596 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060910 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the vector $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -2,4 \\rangle$ shown below.\n\n![](images/cd/cd458eeb41ee09d6a4f58bc343575d46e3d362dc3edca40a47e1a7381fcc9bd2.png)\n\nExpressed in component form, our vector is $\\mathbf{a}=-2\\mathbf{i} + 4 \\mathbf{j}.$\n\nTo find the magnitude (length) of $\\mathbf{a},$ we can use the Pythagorean theorem on $\\triangle OXA.$\n\nThe legs of the triangle have lengths\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{OX}| & =|-2|=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{XA}| & =|\\,4\\,|=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Pythagorean theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{|\\overset{\\to }{OX}{|}^{2}+|\\overset{\\to }{XA}{|}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060910 #edb/ref 1065 2918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060910 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2c0b8c99-c0fd-5bb5-b00d-033a3d589c6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060910 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060911 #edb/ref 1064 "We just saw that the magnitude of the vector $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -2,4 \\rangle$ was given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, given a vector\n![](images/10/10fbddb6dc3528629e5583ad25976d049ca2ec5943ce3e689953f79299b8afcd.svg)\nthe magnitude of the vector can always be computed as\n\n$$\n|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,| = \\sqrt{a_x^2+a_y^2}.\n$$\n\n**Note**\n\nWe sometimes use the notation $|| \\mathbf a ||$ to denote the magnitude of a vector." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060911 #edb/ref 1065 2919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060911 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "60a2e291-183e-53fd-ae24-4840833f4b38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060911 #edb/ref 1067 "General Formula" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501352 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501348 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501352 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501352 #edb/ref 1071 "If $v = ⟨28,-7⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $v$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501352 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "41ade605-a594-51dc-a5e5-aa2a79dd3288" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501352 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501352 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid v \\mid &= \\sqrt{v_{x}^{2} + v_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(28)^{2} + (-7)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{784 + 49} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{833} \\\\\n&= 7 \\sqrt{17}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501357 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501353 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501357 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501357 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $a = ⟨-24,6⟩$. Find $\\mid a \\mid$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501357 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "816d7973-cac7-5db1-9b8c-ad0a12ecb372" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501357 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501357 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a \\mid &= \\sqrt{a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-24)^{2} + (6)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{576 + 36} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{612} \\\\\n&= 6 \\sqrt{17}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501363 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501347 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501363 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501363 #edb/ref 1071 "If $v = ⟨20,-5⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $v$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501363 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "adf1662e-c80f-5fd1-b06c-e22ab1eebd14" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501363 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501363 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid v \\mid &= \\sqrt{v_{x}^{2} + v_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(20)^{2} + (-5)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{400 + 25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{425} \\\\\n&= 5 \\sqrt{17}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501365 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501339 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501365 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501365 #edb/ref 1071 "If $v = ⟨8,-2⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $v$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501365 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b30d0f8c-c583-56ee-9c61-e481453474bb" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501365 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501365 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid v \\mid &= \\sqrt{v_{x}^{2} + v_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(8)^{2} + (-2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{64 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{68} \\\\\n&= 2 \\sqrt{17}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501373 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501351 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501373 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501373 #edb/ref 1071 "If $v = ⟨16,-4⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $v$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501373 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0caf898-ce5d-5506-b145-31d60aeb15df" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501373 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501373 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid v \\mid &= \\sqrt{v_{x}^{2} + v_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(16)^{2} + (-4)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{256 + 16} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{272} \\\\\n&= 4 \\sqrt{17}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501374 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186059714.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501374 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "765ad711-0f93-5cff-882d-5bb7b7ab90a0" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501385 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501386 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501385 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501385 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/07/07a59129f6186959fa9ebad8b924177a81910a3d25c2f292169c41474df99a31.png)\n\nLet $A(-12, 3)$ and $B(9, 0)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501385 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "351db615-bec0-5fbb-9adf-d33132b902d9" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501385 #edb/ref 1073 false #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501385 #edb/ref 1074 "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &= a = - 12 i + 3 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &= b = 9 i.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB} &= \\overrightarrow{OB} - \\overrightarrow{OA} \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (9 i) - (- 12 i + 3 j) \\\\\n&= 21 i - 3 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(21)^{2} + (-3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{441 + 9} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{450} \\\\\n&= 15 \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501390 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501400 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501390 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501390 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/56/5682cc802577e4dd43f42e03bfc829658fc96ca83a15422aa079fe2b43258a0c.png)\n\nLet $A(-8, 2)$ and $B(6, 0)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501390 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "51236f62-ba5d-5c78-8128-0c42c6d77d9b" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501390 #edb/ref 1073 false #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501390 #edb/ref 1074 "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &= a = - 8 i + 2 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &= b = 6 i.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB} &= \\overrightarrow{OB} - \\overrightarrow{OA} \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (6 i) - (- 8 i + 2 j) \\\\\n&= 14 i - 2 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(14)^{2} + (-2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{196 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{200} \\\\\n&= 10 \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501391 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501401 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501391 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501391 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/57/57fd993fac384d9dd76399aa35eec0d9113afeb3c1d24c0a5349d7b4b99df4f1.png)\n\nLet $A(-16, 4)$ and $B(12, 0)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501391 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5b1e6461-4662-5ed4-8cde-319bf158b165" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501391 #edb/ref 1073 false #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501391 #edb/ref 1074 "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &= a = - 16 i + 4 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &= b = 12 i.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB} &= \\overrightarrow{OB} - \\overrightarrow{OA} \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (12 i) - (- 16 i + 4 j) \\\\\n&= 28 i - 4 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(28)^{2} + (-4)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{784 + 16} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{800} \\\\\n&= 20 \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501407 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501387 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501407 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501407 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d7/d7b3f6503172aeab9c4554ffac492a9aab8c16e9ce14f5c552cd1d89dcaa3c66.png)\n\nLet $P(-4, 4)$ and $Q(6, 6)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{PQ}|$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501407 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d8e7cd39-a979-5900-aba6-00ca0310cc42" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501407 #edb/ref 1073 false #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501407 #edb/ref 1074 "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &= p = - 4 i + 4 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OQ} &= q = 6 i + 6 j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{PQ} &= \\overrightarrow{OQ} - \\overrightarrow{OP} \\\\\n&= q - p \\\\\n&= (6 i + 6 j) - (- 4 i + 4 j) \\\\\n&= 10 i + 2 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{PQ}| &= \\sqrt{(10)^{2} + (2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{100 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{104} \\\\\n&= 2 \\sqrt{26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501414 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501402 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501414 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501414 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/6b/6bd80d88ece15997923e5860ff1328dea542c2950c9e4399eba6a5e872070f18.png)\n\nLet $P(-6, 6)$ and $Q(9, 9)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{PQ}|$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501414 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ff8c4899-ff23-5168-90d9-e8d647d7f269" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501414 #edb/ref 1073 false #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501414 #edb/ref 1074 "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &= p = - 6 i + 6 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OQ} &= q = 9 i + 9 j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{PQ} &= \\overrightarrow{OQ} - \\overrightarrow{OP} \\\\\n&= q - p \\\\\n&= (9 i + 9 j) - (- 6 i + 6 j) \\\\\n&= 15 i + 3 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{PQ}| &= \\sqrt{(15)^{2} + (3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{225 + 9} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{234} \\\\\n&= 3 \\sqrt{26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501415 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186059715.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501415 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "76b43aba-c2a9-5fb6-93b1-151df1f6da0b" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501424 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501447 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501424 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501424 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501424 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3fe77d7b-c249-5da3-ae37-3fb1cc69e4ca" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501424 #edb/ref 1073 false #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501424 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a+b &= 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0+(2) \\\\ (-4)+(13)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|2a+b| &= \\sqrt{(2)^2+(9)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{85} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{85}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{85}}\\cdot (2a+b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{85}}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{9 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501425 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501416 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501425 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501425 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501425 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "41db4b75-2005-5439-8a2f-cb0d807696ee" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501425 #edb/ref 1073 false #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501425 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a+b &= 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0+(20) \\\\ (-4)+(-17)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -21\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|2a+b| &= \\sqrt{(20)^2+(-21)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{841} \\\\\n&= 29\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{29}\\cdot (2a+b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{29}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -21\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{20}{29} \\\\ - \\frac{21}{29}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501435 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501441 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186501435 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb